# API proxy: forward /api/* to the API service so the browser talks to a
# single origin (required for the auth cookie to be first-party on Safari).
# Render uses render.yaml for this; the rule below covers Netlify deployments.
/api/*  https://wimapi.onrender.com/api/:splat  200

# SPA fallback: every unknown path serves the React entry so client-side
# routing (React Router) can take over. The 200 status keeps it a regular
# response — not a redirect — so URLs stay intact and the browser doesn't
# show a 3xx flash.
#
# This file is read by Render Static Sites and Netlify. Vite copies it from
# public/ into dist/ verbatim during build. The Docker/nginx build already
# does the same via try_files, so the live site behaves the same regardless
# of which deploy target serves it.
/*    /index.html   200
